  "description": "This is the original animatic for my short film, \"Climb.\" While the final animation evolved during production, this early vision focused much more deeply on the vulnerability of being overwhelmed and the importance of asking for help.\n\nThe baseline of the story explores the parallel stresses of creative work and physical challenges. It follows the main character as they struggle through the burnout of a demanding \"animation project,\" eventually heading to the climbing gym to clear their head—only to find that their \"climbing project\" is just as frustrating.\n\nIn this version, the narrative hits a point where the character feels completely stuck in both worlds, highlighting that suffocating feeling when a problem seems too big to solve alone. The core message is a conversation with a friend who reminds them that seeking advice is not something to be ashamed of. It’s a reminder that we don’t always have to be the sole problem-solvers; instead, we have to recognize the strength it takes to ask for help when we truly need it.",
